WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.208
Row grain is one of the most important design habits
in this

00:00:03.221 --> 00:00:08.764
course Grain answers the question what does one row
represent

00:00:10.479 --> 00:00:15.692
For a patient table one row may represent one
patient For appointment

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:21.086
one row may represent one scheduled encounter For
service one row may

00:00:21.113 --> 00:00:26.758
represent one reusable service definition For
appointment service one row may

00:00:26.784 --> 00:00:32.302
represent one service used during one appointment
Problems begin when

00:00:32.329 --> 00:00:36.039
one row tries to represent several different
subjects at the same time

00:00:37.799 --> 00:00:42.128
Before choosing columns for any table finish the
sentence one row equals

00:00:42.154 --> 00:00:47.384
one what If that sentence is hard to complete the
table design

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:51.621
may be mixing several concepts and should be
reconsidered before implementation
